{
  "name": "winsi-bot",
  "version": "8.9.0",
  "description": "WinsiBot v8.9.0 — High-performance WhatsApp bot with multi-language architecture (TypeScript + Rust + Python), advanced AI, RPG economy, and resilience for very active groups. This release adds two guarantees against lost and duplicated operations. A real outbox: Rust's table recorded deliveries AFTER the fact and without content, so a crash between 'money deducted' and 'confirmation sent' left no trace; it now carries the payload and a queued state, and sendCritical() queues, sends and marks, with replayOutbox() resending on startup and a dead letter after 3 attempts. Applied to the 9 commands where losing the message hurts: transfers (pay/transfer/rob), long-cooldown rewards (daily/weekly/monthly) and settled bets (coinflip/roulette/invest). And message idempotency: Baileys re-delivers messages as 'append' after every reconnect, so a #daily followed by a reconnect ran twice — core/dedup.ts now drops re-deliveries, on disk and scoped per bot instance. Also drops DuckDB (a clean Rust build goes from 10-30 min, and failing outright under MSVC 14.51, to 3m19s), removes 9 dead Rust routes, 3 Python routers and 5 TypeScript client methods, and fixes the credentials backup never doing its final write on shutdown.",
